#
# Counter-example for math:LimitResultShape: a math:LimitResult carrying no
# math:limitOutcome (sh:minCount 1, derived from the exact-one math:limitOutcome
# restriction). Validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent
# (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult). It carries no math:limitResultValue either, so
# the outcome↔value agreement constraint stays vacuously satisfied and the missing
# required outcome is the single isolated violation. Bound by
# ex:ecLimitResultMissingOutcome.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:outcomelessResult a math:LimitResult ;
    rdfs:label "A limit result asserted without naming its outcome"@x-gmeow-english .
